cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Explainable Credit Scorecard Framework: Weight of Evidence logistic regression scorecard for lenders serving applicants with thin or no credit bureau file"
authors:
  - family-names: Asare
    given-names: Prince Akonor
    affiliation: Get Credit Rate Foundation
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-18
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/getcreditrate/scorecard
url: https://getcreditrate.com
abstract: >
  Open-source Weight of Evidence logistic regression scorecard for Community Development
  Financial Institutions and other regulated lenders, validated on 1,249,246 resolved
  consumer loans with an out-of-time test on 462,426 loans. With every credit report field
  removed, eight application-level characteristics retain 81.9 percent of the benchmark
  Gini. Includes a pre-registered retrospective validation protocol, fair-lending test
  implementation and model risk governance documentation. Released under the Apache
  License 2.0 by Get Credit Rate Foundation, a Delaware nonprofit corporation.
keywords:
  - credit scoring
  - weight of evidence
  - logistic regression
  - fair lending
  - explainable machine learning
  - community development financial institutions
  - alternative data
  - model risk management
